{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_supervision_supervision", "label": "Supervision", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "A failure in onReceive does not crash the process: it travels to the parent, which decides. A supervisor one level up has a wider view than the call site \u2014 it knows whether the crashed actor is replaceable, holds critical state, or should give up.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/supervision.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_supervision_let_it_crash", "label": "Let it crash", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Inherited from Erlang. Handling every error inline at the call site is brittle; restart explicitly does not preserve in-memory state because the philosophy trusts the recovery path more than the per-message guard.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/supervision.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_supervision_directive", "label": "Directive", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "The decider returns one of four outcomes \u2014 Restart, Resume, Stop, Escalate \u2014 picked per error class.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/supervision.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_supervision_restart_directive", "label": "Restart directive", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "The framework default. The broken instance is dropped and rebuilt from the same class or factory; the mailbox is retained and the failed message is dropped. Instance fields are lost by design \u2014 state that must survive belongs in a journal or DistributedData.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/supervision.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_supervision_resume_directive", "label": "Resume directive", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Keeps state and skips the failing message \u2014 right for transient errors (network blip, brief DB unavailability). Wrong when the state itself caused the throw, because the next message fails the same way.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/supervision.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_supervision_oneforonestrategy", "label": "OneForOneStrategy", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Applies the directive to just the failing child; siblings keep running. The default, and what the vast majority of actor-ts code uses \u2014 one user-session crashing should not affect the others.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/supervision.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_supervision_allforonestrategy", "label": "AllForOneStrategy", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Applies the directive to every child when any one fails. Reserved for children whose states are explicitly coupled \u2014 a producer/consumer pair over an internal channel.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/supervision.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_supervision_decideby", "label": "decideBy", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Builds a per-error decider from a list of error-class-to-directive mappings plus a fallback, so different error classes get different responses without hand-writing the decider function.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/supervision.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_supervision_stopchildrenonrestart", "label": "stopChildrenOnRestart", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Children are stopped on restart because the alternative broke an ordinary pattern: postRestart re-runs preStart, so an actor that spawned a named child there hit 'Child name is not unique' on its first restart. It is a separate hook rather than a preRestart override because the teardown must be awaited \u2014 the new instance cannot be built while the old children still hold their names. Opting out requires an idempotent preStart that adopts the survivor from the cell, not from an instance field.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/supervision.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_supervision_defaultstrategy", "label": "defaultStrategy", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Restart everything, capped at 10 per minute. The cap exists precisely to break the infinite restart loop a child crashing on permanently-broken state would otherwise produce. Note the parent-side counter is inclusive of the failure that trips it.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/supervision.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_supervision_behaviors_supervise", "label": "Behaviors.supervise().onFailure", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "The typed wrapper honours maxRetries and withinTimeRangeMs but reads maxRetries literally and escalates past the bound rather than stopping. It has to: the wrapper lives inside the failing actor, not in a parent that stays around to observe the death, so stopping there would discard the error with nobody upstream the wiser.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/supervision.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_supervision_escalation_chain", "label": "Escalation chain", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Escalation walks up the parent tree to the root user guardian; if that escalates too the system enters a fatal-error state. So uncaught errors only happen when every level explicitly chooses to escalate \u2014 stops are a normal outcome, escalation-to-root is the 'we do not know what to do' signal.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/supervision.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_supervision_let_it_crash", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_supervision_supervision", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/supervision.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_supervision_supervision", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_supervision_directive", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/supervision.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_supervision_directive", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_supervision_restart_directive", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/supervision.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_supervision_directive", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_supervision_resume_directive", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/supervision.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_supervision_let_it_crash", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_supervision_restart_directive", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/supervision.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_supervision_oneforonestrategy", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_supervision_directive", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/supervision.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_supervision_allforonestrategy", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_supervision_directive", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/supervision.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_supervision_oneforonestrategy", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_supervision_allforonestrategy", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/supervision.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_supervision_decideby", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_supervision_oneforonestrategy", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/supervision.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_supervision_defaultstrategy", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_supervision_restart_directive", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/supervision.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_supervision_stopchildrenonrestart", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_supervision_restart_directive", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/supervision.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_supervision_behaviors_supervise", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_supervision_escalation_chain", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/supervision.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_supervision_behaviors_supervise", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_supervision_defaultstrategy", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "AMBIGUOUS", "confidence_score": 0.25, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/supervision.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_supervision_escalation_chain", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_supervision_directive", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/supervision.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_supervision_supervision", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_timers_and_scheduling_timerscheduler", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/supervision.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}], "hyperedges": []}